WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.125
This practice changes only the reference date in the
recent respiratory report

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.512
Replace August 11, 2026 with August 5, 2026 and
think about the new thirty-day

00:00:10.538 --> 00:00:16.412
window Before running identify which admissions are
near the boundaries Moving

00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:19.938
the reference date earlier changes which dates
qualify but it does not

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.462
change patient ages or the age-sixty risk threshold
This separation is important

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:31.162
The WHERE clause defines the cohort The CASE
expression classifies the rows

00:00:31.188 --> 00:00:35.750
that remain A change to the population does not
automatically change the

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:40.975
classification rule After predicting run the revised
query and compare the set

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.900
of admissions with the original result
